{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"errata","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1012"},"reason":"a1012 bodyEn/De paragraph 2: PKS went on air from a basement studio (not \"a small studio\"); \"roughly 1,200 cable households\" → \"the still small audience of cable households\" (unverified; 2,600 households were connected by March 1984); \"New Year's concert\" → Handel's Royal Fireworks music; dropped \"when it began transmitting by satellite\" (unverified); RTL plus started in a studio in Bertrange, not the Villa Louvigny, and its first viewers got it through the Dudelange transmitter (this backs printed wording w11815) — https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sat.1, https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/RTL_Television, https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabelpilotprojekt","by":"enrich batch 061","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a2248-a2251.md","sources":[{"url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sat.1"},{"url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/RTL_Television"},{"url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabelpilotprojekt"}]},
